 lists, activates, or deactivates the packages this repository takes

   list    prints every package in reach, with a ✅ beside the active ones and a ❌ beside the
           excluded ones, its origin (release or repository), and its description. This is the
           default.
   select  makes exactly the named packages, with the packages they depend on and the members they
           include, the active set: it removes what the set omits, adds what it lacks, and says
           which active package it kept for another's sake; with nothing to change it says the set
   add     activates the packages, the packages they depend on, and the members they include, places
           the files they deliver, and rewrites the manifests. When a different file is already at a
           delivered path, it is named and left alone, and no manifest is written. A package named
           here is no longer excluded.
   remove  takes out what the packages delivered (files, the kit's JSON entries, and the kit's
           regions) and rewrites the manifests. A package that an active package depends on is
           refused. A member of a bundle that stays active is recorded as excluded, so that kit
           update does not bring it back.


 kit package
